-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt browser playground
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/), compiled from C++ to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The original Monte Carlo radiance integrator, Cornell box, mirror, and glass materials are retained. The browser adaptation adds progressive RGBA output and editable material colors.
 
+## Build
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm build
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+The compiled WebAssembly and its loader are committed under `public/wasm/`. A normal app build does not require Emscripten. To rebuild the binary after editing `native/smallpt.cpp`, install Emscripten and run:
 
-## Tech Stack
+```sh
+pnpm build:wasm
+```
+
+The homepage is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`. The existing Astro Node adapter remains available for other routes. Assets and the worker are served from the same origin. Rendering requires no server API, cross-origin isolation, or SharedArrayBuffer.
+
+## Rendering
+
+`public/wasm/render-worker.js` loads the compiled C++ module in a dedicated worker. Each pass traces four samples per pixel using smallpt’s 2×2 subpixel sampling. It reports progress and transfers RGBA frames to the canvas. Starting another render terminates the old worker. Palette edits, sample counts, and resolution changes render again; the randomize button changes both walls and sphere tints. Images can be saved as PNG.
+
+`public/images/smallpt-preview.png` is a 256-sample rendering generated by the same C++ source, used while the first live pass loads. It is replaced by live WebAssembly output. It is not a substitute for the renderer.
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+`native/smallpt.original.cpp` preserves the upstream source. smallpt is distributed under Kevin Beason’s MIT license, included in `native/LICENSE.txt` and `public/wasm/LICENSE.txt`.
